From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0015] ANE_FRONTEND_SPEC: correct the write_state contradiction

The document contradicted itself on what `write_state` accepts:

  line 59  : "write_state(data=X, input=st) accepts any tensor X of matching
              type"
  line ~281: "write_state(data=X, input=st) accepts ONLY state-derived X"

Measured on h17 with mil_infer/examples/probe_run2_state.rs (5 independent
cases), the strict reading wins and the lax one is simply wrong — it does not
even hold on the same aned build it was written about:

  case 1  write_state(data = bare read_state result)        REJECTED
  case 2  full-arg slice_update -> write su                 ACCEPTED
  case 3  same, output the pre-write read_state (readback)  ACCEPTED
  case 4  two states, one triple each                       ACCEPTED
  case 5  write_state(data = read_state) with live su       REJECTED

So there is no "any tensor" case at all: data must be the terminal
slice_update output. Even a pure passthrough with no slice_update in the
program is refused.

Both bullets now state the same rule. The corrections are marked inline
rather than silently rewritten, so a reader arriving from the old text can see
what changed and why, and each carries a pointer to
docs/evidence/RUN-2-state-lifecycle.md section 3.

Doc-only change; no code references these lines (searched).

Found during RUN-2 (L-RUN), patched at the lane owner's direction.
Upstream: 20f097fb34969cd577342a4d7996fbf5464998c8
